<% content_for :title, "Read a passport" %>

<h1>Read a passport</h1>

<p class="lede">
  The two lines of letters and chevrons along the bottom of the photo page. Point a camera at them or
  copy them in, and we will fill the form for you — including the expiry date, which is the part
  people most often mistype.
</p>

<% if @result && !@result.valid? %>
  <div class="errors" role="alert" tabindex="-1">
    <strong>That did not read cleanly:</strong>
    <ul>
      <% @result.errors.each do |message| %>
        <li><%= message %></li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      Every field in that zone carries a check digit, so we can tell when a character has been
      misread rather than storing a wrong date and reminding you on the wrong day.
    </p>
  </div>
<% end %>

<%# The camera and the box it fills have to sit inside one controller element, %>
<%# so the form is wrapped too rather than living beside it. %>
<div data-controller="mrz">
  <section>
    <h2>Point a camera at it</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Nothing is uploaded. The frame is read in your browser and dropped — only the characters you
      submit ever reach us.
    </p>

    <div class="capture">
      <video data-mrz-target="video" playsinline muted hidden aria-label="Camera preview"></video>
      <img data-mrz-target="still" hidden alt="The captured zone, magnified for copying">
      <canvas data-mrz-target="canvas" hidden></canvas>
    </div>

    <p>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-quiet" data-mrz-target="start" data-action="mrz#start">
        Use the camera
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="btn" data-mrz-target="capture" data-action="mrz#capture" hidden>
        Capture
      </button>
    </p>

    <p class="note" data-mrz-target="status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

    <noscript>
      <p class="note">The camera needs JavaScript. Typing the lines in below works without it.</p>
    </noscript>
  </section>

  <%= form_with url: scans_path, method: :post do |form| %>
    <div class="field">
      <%= form.label :mrz, "Machine-readable zone" %>
      <p class="hint">
        Two lines of 44 characters for a passport, three lines of 30 for an ID card. Include the
        &lt; characters.
      </p>
      <%= form.text_area :mrz, rows: 4, value: params[:mrz], autofocus: true,
            spellcheck: false, autocapitalize: "characters", class: "mono",
            data: { mrz_target: "input" },
            placeholder: "P<NPLBHATTARAI<<RAJAN<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<\n12AB345676NPL9001152M3102201<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<4" %>
    </div>

    <%= form.submit "Read it", class: "btn" %>
    <%= link_to "Type it in instead", new_document_path, class: "btn btn-quiet" %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<section class="provenance">
  <h2>What happens to it</h2>
  <p>
    The zone is parsed and discarded. It carries a name, a sex and a date of birth, none of which we
    need to work out a renewal date, so none of them are stored — we keep the document kind, the
    issuing country and the expiry date, and you can edit all three before saving.
  </p>
</section>
